What was changed (PRD v2 §8)
----------------------------
- A4 by default; modern CV limit 2 pages instead of 1; a traditional Sri Lankan style (personal details,
  O/L and A/L result tables, two non-related referees, NIC only when the ad requires it) with no page limit.
- File name Firstname_Lastname_Role.pdf instead of firstname-lastname-resume.pdf.
- The "background dossier" became user/resume.md + user/facts.yml; facts are written only with
  `slj facts add --confirmed` after the person confirms the wording.
- The fact gate is the deterministic `slj factcheck` (src/cv/factcheck.ts), which also rejects tools and
  qualifications copied from the job ad, and blocks `slj cv render` until it passes.
- resume-optimizer's match-analysis scoring was removed; the gap analysis reuses the project's star rubric
  (modes/score.md) so the top-20 stars and the CV flow agree.
- Nothing Claude-only on the required path: the reviewer subagent is optional; the in-context review is
  a first-class path. No plugin agent definition is shipped.
- All Python script calls (render.py, ats-check.py, html-to-md.py) were replaced by `slj` commands.
  Rendering uses Playwright with an empty header template and a srilankanjobs.lk footer watermark; the
  "derive the Markdown from the HTML" rule is replaced by one-way generation cv.md -> HTML -> PDF.
- Removed: portfolio-link harvesting, company research, cover-letter skill, US conventions (work
  authorisation, Letter paper, US section names), the multi-job leverage section of branching-questions.md.
- Added Sri Lankan question types and the one-question-at-a-time / stop-at-about-8 rule.

